  "body": "Small PR, first of two: the Home Assistant tile only. Based on current `main`, no other file touched.\n\n## What it adds\n\nA virtual **Home** tile, built the same way as the launcher's own Settings and Sources tiles: it opens a Home Assistant dashboard in Internet.\n\n- `launcher/js/homeassistant.js`: `APL.ha` — reads the address, opens it, refuses anything that isn't `http(s)`, and shows the same \"would open in Internet\" toast as a web app in the PC preview.\n- `launcher/js/launcher.js`: the `apl.homeassistant` virtual app, plus one small addition to `buildList()` — a virtual app can now carry `when`, so this tile exists only on an installation that set it up (`needs` already did the same for TizenTube).\n- `launcher/js/settings-tree.js`: Settings › Apps › **Home Assistant** — Configured / Missing.\n- `launcher/images/apps/homekit-tile.png`: the orange HomeKit-style tile.\n- `tools/make-build.py` + regenerated `build.js` / `version.json`.\n\n## Where the address lives\n\nNot in the repo, and not in Settings: a dashboard URL names the house, sometimes carries a token. It goes in `js/keys.local.js`, next to the TMDB / YouTube / Fanart keys that are already per-install:\n\n```js\nwindow.APL_KEYS = {\n    ha: { url: \"http://homeassistant.local:8123/lovelace/tv\", name: \"Home\" }\n};\n```\n\nWithout it there is **no tile at all** — nothing to explain to someone who doesn't run Home Assistant, and nothing personal in the public code. `name` is optional (defaults to \"Home\").\n\n## To test on the screen\n\n1. Add the `ha:` line above to `js/keys.local.js`, build, install.\n2. The Home tile sits in the dock after the favourites; OK opens the dashboard in Internet, Home comes back to the launcher.\n3. Remove the line: the tile is gone again after a restart, and nothing else changes.\n\nSettings › Home Screen › Show on Home Screen and hold-OK › Hide App work on it like on any other tile.\n\nThe Home Assistant app itself (rooms, lights, scenes drawn by the launcher) is not in this PR: it is a lot of code and I'd rather you see the tile first.\n",
